<title>BELGIUM: Neuhaus up 20 pct at first bourse fixing.</title>
<headline>Neuhaus up 20 pct at first bourse fixing.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian chocolate maker Neuhaus started at 2,100 Belgian francs on its first day of trade on the Brussels Stock Exchange on Tuesday, twenty percent higher than its initial public offer price.</p>
<p>Neuhaus's controlling shareholder  Artal Nederland BV sold 450,000 shares to the public in an IPO last month at 1,750 francs each. The shares are quoted on the bourse's twice-daily fixed cash market, where prices are fixed at 1100 and 1500 local (1000 GMT and 1400 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
